      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unaligned access on bloonchipper is slower for both tests. Is this intended?\n\n```\n\u003e runtest\nRunning test_unaligned_access...\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nPass: *test_array_ptr \u003d\u003d expected_results[i]\nOK\nRunning benchmark_unaligned_access_memcpy...\n (speed gain: 11053 -\u003e 3772 us) OK\nRunning benchmark_unaligned_access_array...\n (speed gain: 4514 -\u003e 4141 us) OK\nPass!\n```\n\nAlso, do note that we are still compiling with `-mno-unaligned-access`.",
      "revId": "95b3153191303fdd76f4d874cf11683b298d157c",
