      "writtenOn": "2023-07-14T21:55:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Without giving it much thought, I think you\u0027re right. As long as you run enough iterations for the small delta to be accurately measurable, I think it converges to the same conclusion.\n\nI think when it comes down any *issues* here, I think it is mainly a disagreement about findings presentation. It wasn\u0027t obvious from looking at the total `us` how much faster one was over the other. This could easily be fixes.\n\nAnother issue with my approach is that a good cache that saves unaligned accesses can make this since access non-existent. This might totally break down on dartmonkey. I\u0027m good with submitting, but we probably want a benchmark similar to yours in the future.",
