      "side": 1,
      "message": "By default, `memcpy` is designed to never make unaligned accesses, even when you give it unaligned starting address. Most implementations will do byte-by-byte copies until it can switch to aligned faster word copies.\n\nThe implementation being used here (a mirror of it):\n* [Pretty mirror of newlib-4.1.0](https://github.com/bminor/newlib/blob/newlib-4.1.0/newlib/libc/machine/arm/memcpy-armv7m.S#L189)\n* [Non-pretty upstream newlib-4.1.0](https://sourceware.org/git/?p\u003dnewlib-cygwin.git;a\u003dblob;f\u003dnewlib/libc/machine/arm/memcpy-armv7m.S;h\u003dc8bff36f60cf6ed520172c85406f6a9529f41de3;hb\u003d415fdd4279b85eeec9d54775ce13c5c412451e08)\n\nThe C version we used to use in EC:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/builtin/stdlib.c;l\u003d302",
